The DoWorkAsync method is already virtual (it overrides a virtual method from the base class), so I can subclass BackgroundJobWorker in the test and override DoWorkAsync if needed. However, since the method is protected override, I cannot call it directly from the test. Instead, I will test the public behavior by triggering the background worker's work cycle or by invoking the base class method that calls DoWorkAsync.

I will create a test that mocks IServiceProvider to verify that GetRequiredService<IBackgroundJobStore>() is called. I will also mock the other dependencies to allow the method to run without exceptions.

I will submit a test file that covers the call to GetRequiredService on IServiceProvider in DoWorkAsync.

